---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const DEMO_URL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_DEMO_URL || 'https://shoreline-demo.onrender.com/menu'
---

<BaseLayout title="Founder Story — Built by an Healthcare Executive Chef in Maine" description="Why ShorelineOps was created inside a real senior living kitchen dealing with dysphagia textures, allergen risks, and food distributor ordering.">
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="text-center mb-12 sm:mb-16">
        <div class="inline-block px-3.5 py-1 bg-teal-50 dark:bg-teal-950/70 border border-teal-200/70 dark:border-teal-800/60 rounded-full text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 font-mono shadow-2xs">
          Practitioner-Led Healthcare Dining
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-4 leading-tight">
          Why I Built ShorelineOps Inside a Real Senior Living Kitchen.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 italic">
          "Nobody selling healthcare dietary software has ever cooked a pureed dinner service for 80 residents with 14 different allergy restrictions while balancing food cost."
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Story Narrative Body -->
      <div class="space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        
        <p>
          If you have ever stepped into a senior living dietary department at 4:30 PM, you know the daily high-stakes reality:
        </p>
        
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50/60 dark:bg-amber-950/30 border border-amber-200/60 dark:border-amber-900/40 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-300 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-mono">The Daily 4:30 PM Rush</div>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-600 font-bold">1.</span>
              <span><strong>Last-Minute Clinical Changes:</strong> Nursing calls down right before tray line with two room transfers, a new physician Low Sodium diet order, and a resident newly designated NPO awaiting swallow evaluation.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-600 font-bold">2.</span>
              <span><strong>Kitchen Ergonomics Under Fire:</strong> Line cooks with wet nitrile gloves are trying to read faded handwriting on a greasy whiteboard while staging 4 pans of hot entrees.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
              <span class="text-amber-600 font-bold">3.</span>
              <span><strong>Clipboard Inventory Guesswork:</strong> Building weekly orders for <strong>Dennis Food Service</strong> or <strong>Sysco</strong> using clipboards and guesswork, hoping you don't stock out of thickener or pureed meats before Friday truck delivery.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4">The Legacy Industry Dilemma</h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
          When I looked across the commercial software landscape, I found two deeply frustrating options:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-4">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-apple-subtle">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mb-1">1. Proprietary Monopolies ($1,200+/mo)</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Bulky software designed for 500-bed hospital chains, bloated with unnecessary complexity, requiring 6 months of onboarding, and locking you into a single distributor.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-apple-subtle">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mb-1">2. Paper Binders & Spreadsheets</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">What 80% of independent and assisted living homes actually use because commercial software is unaffordable, resulting in human error and survey anxiety.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white pt-4">The ShorelineOps Vision: Open Core + Clinical Precision</h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
          I built <strong>ShorelineOps</strong> to be the tool I needed in the kitchen every single morning:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>100% Free Open-Source Core:</strong> Any independent care home, hospice, or non-profit assisted living community can run our software completely free. Clinical safety should never be paywalled.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>Big, High-Contrast Touch Targets (44px+):</strong> Touch tablet kiosk mode designed specifically for gloved line cooks to tap easily during hot line service.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>IDDSI 2.0 Hard-Blocks:</strong> Strict clinical safety rules preventing a Regular texture plate from ever being served to an IDDSI Level 4 Pureed resident.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold">✓</span>
            <span><strong>Algorithmic Split MRP Purchasing:</strong> Automatically compares line-item contract quotes across Dennis Food Service, Sysco, and US Foods, saving $1.50–$3.00 per resident day.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- Visual Real Screenshot of Tablet -->
        <div class="my-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 shadow-apple-subtle">
          <img src="/screenshots/kitchen_tablet_kiosk.png" alt="Shoreline Touch Tablet Kiosk" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" />
        </div>

        <!-- Contact Box -->
        <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800/80 my-8 text-center shadow-apple-card">
          <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2 font-sans">Let’s Talk Culinary & Dietary Operations</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-xs sm:text-sm max-w-lg mx-auto mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            Whether you are a Dietary Manager in New England or an Executive Director looking to tighten food spend and survey readiness, we would love to show you ShorelineOps.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3">
            <a
              href={DEMO_URL}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
              class="w-full sm:w-auto px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-xs sm:text-sm transition-all shadow-sm shadow-blue-600/30"
            >
              Launch Interactive Demo App &rarr;
            </a>
            <a
              href="/distributors"
              class="w-full sm:w-auto px-6 py-3 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 font-semibold rounded-xl text-xs sm:text-sm hover:bg-slate-200 transition-all"
            >
              For Food Distributors (Dennis & Sysco)
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
